            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="1122" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">755.93/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-27T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 27—9:37
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>356. Your 173, August 24, 6 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d764-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Belgian Minister confidentially informs me his Government advises him that
                        it contemplates simultaneous action by the Washington Conference powers “in
                        order to obtain a basis for an acceptable <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                            vivendi.</hi>” If any such action should be taken at all (against which
                        I still strongly advise) it seems to me that it should be in the sense of a
                        protest against China’s violation of Belgian treaty rights rather than of an
                        attempt to influence the terms of the proposed <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                            vivendi</hi> which is a matter of friendly concession by the Belgian
                        Government and does not involve any question of principle.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I beg to request that you advise me of such action as you may decide to
                        take upon the Belgian note.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
